# Pairs with NoKeyLost. A fold's survivor can hold the saga's other buckets;
# applying the terminal there must drain them all. Here the sweep backstops k2
# only, yet records the terminal as applied, so the survivor's k1 bucket is
# discarded when the broadcast arrives and k1 loses the committed batch.
MODULE: NoKeyLostFoldSweepDrainsOnlyMovedKey
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the decided sweep marks the survivor's activation as having applied the terminal but drains only the moved key's bucket
PERTURBS: MigSweep

--- FIND
                                       IF k = k2 \/ (pend[dst][k] # "none" /\ ~term[dst])
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: only the moved key is drained.
                                       IF k = k2
--- END
